# equal-weight point: cut at the valley of P(k), P(k < cut) = 1/2
#   80 bins of width dk = 0.00174865; smoothing resolution m = 30: moving average over 3 bins (dk window = 0.00524594)
# s_equal g 0 s* nan kcut nan err nan (0/30 replicas)  (no two-peak valley or not bracketed by target_s)
# peaks: averages within each peak at the equal-weight point s*
#   inactive: k < kcut, active: k >= kcut; dk = k_act - k_in, de = e_act - e_in
#   sdk_in, sdk_act: standard deviation of k within the peak
#   err_*: std over the bootstrap replicas, each at its own s* and kcut; nrep = replicas used
#   columns: g s* kcut k_in k_act dk e_in e_act de sdk_in sdk_act err_k_in err_k_act err_dk err_e_in err_e_act err_de nrep
# peaks 0 nan nan nan nan nan nan nan nan nan nan nan nan nan nan nan nan 0
